<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>TypeScript</language>
Generate src/explore.ts as a bounded browser orchestrator for the approved mathematical-physics exploration story. Mount an explorable world and a genuine Rust-backed SU(2) laboratory with linked plots, axes, t in radians with play/pause/scrub/step/reset/checkpoints, slice control and versioned local journal. Use /api/su2, preserve U versus -U, display numerical evidence status never proof. Never recompute mathematical kernel results in the UI or label stale plots current. Cancel stale requests and animation on dispose. State persistence is independent of notebook and style, with unsupported data retained for export and explicit reset. Pin/reopen/compare journal entries and export/import versioned state with source references. Context buttons and keyboard/direct lab entry must work without avatar traversal. Views supplied by explore-plots.ts and world by explore-world.ts. Source linking and notebook pinning use callbacks, no filesystem writes. Readable numeric matrices and projection equations, poles and slice status. Network errors visible. Original game art only. Future QFT destinations clearly unavailable, not implemented simulations. No provider-backed automated regeneration is claimed.

Playback must avoid abort-starving slow requests: sample absolute time only when the previous calculation is complete, and label checked results only for the exact currently displayed input. Pause persists the selected angle; edits do not get overwritten by playback. Preserve in-memory journal entries on quota/blocked-storage failure, report they are unsaved, and allow export. Async import must abandon disposed views.

The mounted view exposes exportState() so the shared Ctrl/Cmd+S command exports the exploration when Explore is active, preserving current notebook export behavior on exit.

Superseding separation requirement: Explore is a standalone game-first application. Remove pinNotebook and any notebook callback or UI. Optional source/openSource callbacks come from its own field guide. Export discoveries as data; no notebook cells/tabs or pin actions. Keep existing exploration storage and imported source references. Notebook interoperability is future optional file exchange, not a required interaction.

Superseding scene-first correction: mountScene supplies the primary interactive laboratory viewport. Default lab contains only scene, compact HUD and contextual Rotate/Slice/Play/Keep tools; all matrix/plots/precision controls are in native modal Scan. Field journal and future atlas open on request. Usercanmanipulateangle/slice directly withoutopeningScan. Preserve previous math,state,reference,exports and stale-result handling. Dialogclose/Escape restorefocus; disposaldestroysdialogs,scene,network,timers. Never equate visual milestones with mathematical proof.

Playful intuitive polish: original tool pictograms keep visible labels and ARIA names. R/S/Space/K shortcuts act only when the scene canvas owns focus and no modifiers; never steal text/scan controls. A requested Tips speech panel offers one-turn2pi andtwo-turn4pi experiments, usesactualRuststate anddoesnotgate tools. Keep discovery duringpending/playing waitsfortheexactclickedinput; cancels onchangedpoint/error ratherthansavinganotherstate. Successfulrecording has brief decorativefeedback anddistinctopt-in sound; quotafailure remainsunsaved/inmemory. Clean timers/listeners/dialogs ondispose. ReferenceCSS/repos arestartingpoints, notbindingdesignlibraries.
